                <pb facs="0664" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg568"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Sorsby.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Claim all exemptions, privileges, and immunities accorded by Nicaragua by treaty
                    to consuls of any other most favored foreign nation. If none such are accorded
                    by treaty between Nicaragua and other foreign State, Clancy may testify touching
                    facts which came to his knowledge in his merely personal and unofficial
                    capacity, but not as to facts or communications obtained in his capacity as
                    consular agent. If he so testifies, report to the Department copy of questions
                    and answers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
